      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Meaning of Industry"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Industry encompasses economic activities involved in the extraction, processing, and manufacturing of raw materials.",
        "Industries are categorized according to raw materials, operational size, ownership structure, and economic roles.",
        "Geographical distribution of industries depends on raw materials, power supply, labor force, market access, and transport networks.",
        "Industrial policy evolution plays a crucial role in shaping public and private manufacturing sectors in India."
      ],
      "id": "2dqol39"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "v8oswwu",
      "content": "• Industry refers to economic activities related to the production of goods."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ahvkoln",
      "content": "• It involves the conversion of raw materials into finished products."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "j9pfflm",
      "content": "• Industries help in increasing production and economic growth."
    },
